// The handler that serves the arm's ask is installed INSIDE the asking
// handler's extent: hf's arm performs `op`, and `he` sits under hf. The arm
// resolves outer of hf, where no E handler is; the row says exactly that
// (row(hf) carries E past the inner install to the root). Refused. The boot
// accepted it and the run aborted at the walk.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect F { f_op() -> Int }
handler hf { f_op() => resume(op() + 1) }
handler he { op() => resume(10) }
fn main() = (f_op()) ~> he ~> hf
